    "Bounds-check all shader instruction-format tables; undefined/outside entries retain explicit decoder rejection, with valid metadata unchanged.",
    "Complete SH register destination bounds and opt-in bounded program-address write/lookup provenance; metadata failure saves exact scanned bytes without a second backing read.",
    "Pass bounded original PM4 packet spans to shader-address tracing; retain post-copy raw register and original SET_SH_REG address pair without additional guest reads.",
    "Bound compute PM4 framing before copies; preserve multi-part ring packets and isolate complete indirect buffers. CPU controls only; native shader-origin cause remains unresolved.",
    "Opt-in bounded pre-enqueue shader-head and original address-pair observations, retained per submission through decoding and persisted in independent submission/consumption journal tails. No shader acceptance or guest ownership change.",
    "Optional bounded shader-prefix overlap observations at generic emulator GPU-write intent sites, independent of the upstream allocator/free-list diagnostic setting. No write, allocator assumption or success substitution.",
    "Distinguish classic, paged, storage-image and render-target writable shader bindings; observe exact guest ranges without changing descriptors, barriers, invalidation or GPU ordering.",
    "Observe a distinct resolved storage-image backing range only when overlap/subresource resolution differs from the requested descriptor; no image, view, barrier or ordering change.",
    "Backport runtime 41f289fe81e0 display-view lifetime: cache presenter views with the display image, keyed by format and alpha mapping; retain local image ownership and synchronization. No backend migration or shader metadata bypass.",
    "Full October 25 runtime/CPU migration; backend device resource ownership, cached shader compatibility, memory events and SotC diagnostics adapted. Cache 29/9 separates previous generated shaders.",
    "October26 runtime a27f0ca native Metal startup and capability migration. SotC shader/memory/diagnostic patches preserved; CPU translator remains196ed99 via explicit submodule override.",
    "Opt-in GPU rebasing of direct indexed draws whose index extent exceeds 4 GiB; bounds checked, scratch retained through completion, indirect draws unchanged.",
    "Opt-in GPU-only indexed indirect normalization, ordered reusable 8 MiB workspace, argument preservation and explicit completion-time invalid/capacity failure; no early submission or CPU argument readback.",
    "Opt-in selective indirect index copy: GPU-validated low ranges use original indices; mutually exclusive low/copy argument records preserve order; completed-command copy counters.",
    "Backport runtime 82051e5bc970: reject Metal block-texel views and keep incompatible compressed/uncompressed cache images separate, including overlapping mips and slices. Vulkan capability retained.",
    "October28 full runtime 73672843f513 and CPU c47af50ed8f8 migration; all prior SotC corrections three-way merged. Block-texel fix now upstream. Locked library recipe retained to avoid downgrading previously updated packages.",
    "October29 runtime994846bb/CPU4d9c384 migration; preserve SotC overlays, unique shader permutation indices, cached environment lookup, game-thread QoS. Cache30/9 rejects previous shader identities.",
